.env
/config.php

# User-uploaded content (product/variation images) - must never be tracked, and must never
# be touched by any git-based clean/reset operation a deployment runs. See
# includes/image_upload.php's image_upload_base_dir() for where this is written at runtime.
# ROOT CAUSE (see investigation): this directory was NOT excluded before, and this repo's
# automated commit-on-change history showed production's config.php being overwritten within
# minutes of a local edit here - proving an active deploy pipeline exists. If that pipeline
# resets the target directory to match this git tree (a full re-clone/rsync --delete style
# deploy, not a plain in-place `git pull`), every deploy wipes every previously uploaded
# image, because nothing under uploads/ was ever tracked and .gitignore didn't protect it
# from a clean/reset step either. Excluding it here is necessary but may not be SUFFICIENT -
# if the deploy mechanism does a full directory replace rather than an in-place git
# pull/clean, uploads/ must also be explicitly preserved/excluded in that deploy
# configuration itself (outside this repo), or moved to a location the deploy never touches.
/uploads

/vendor

/node_modules

/storage/logs

/storage/temp

.DS_Store

Thumbs.db